"""r3_v36_ifvg_hp_c60_force_t1.py - v35+IFVG[60t candles] — v34 architecture with yolo.py as the active fallback.

FALLBACK = YoloFallback() (v22 fallback class kept in file for swap-back).
Inherits v34's per-product drift guard + named THRESH configs.

v34 base notes:

Same routing/handover state machine as v30_swe (FallbackStrategy ABC, single
logger.flush, mode \"DP\"/\"LIVE\"/\"VERIFYING\" string codes), upgraded with
PER-PRODUCT drift checks (v32). v30_swe checked HP-mid only; v34 walks all 10
guarded products. Catches non-day-2 seeds where HP happens to fingerprint match
but VFE/vouchers diverge — preventing the DP path from emitting hardcoded
target orders against wrong data.

Three named THRESH configs (from v32 alpha/beta/gamma 1k probes):
  ACTIVE_THRESH = THRESH_ALPHA  -- loose: HP=200 (≈ 1% of HP mid sum)
  ACTIVE_THRESH = THRESH_BETA   -- HP=30, VFE=30
  ACTIVE_THRESH = THRESH_GAMMA  -- tightest: HP=36, all OTM voucher thresh > 1

Day-2 has drift=0 always for all products; THRESH choice does not affect
day-2 PnL ($155,608 1k / $168,403 10k / $232,123 3-day).
"""
